    Look request (temporary): a chat's title in the rule above the box
    
    The user, trying the launchpad on a real box (2026-11-08): the chat's
    top line ("✦ Vsr / hello T4 ... 127.0.0.1:8367") takes the screen's
    first row. It moves into the rule above the box, aligned right as
    Claude Code's is, freeing that row for the conversation, as
    launchpad-chat/04 shows:
    
        ────────────────────────────────── Hello / What can you tell… T2 on box:40691 ──
        ❯ Reply
    
    - The rule carries the project, " / ", the chat's title, its number,
      and " on " and the engine's place, then two dashes to the right edge.
      The "✦" goes with the top line.
    - The title is cut to at most 20 characters, at a word where it can be,
      ending in "…".
    - The engine's place is "box" when the TUI runs on a temper box at its
      default port (8367), "box:PORT" on a box at another port, and
      HOST:PORT otherwise.
    - The conversation starts on the first row.
    
    States the frame doesn't show:
    - A narrow terminal: the place goes first, then the project.
    - While a list is open under the box (commands, a question), the rule
      above the box keeps the title.
    - The light theme, by the same tokens.
    
    Replaces: the chat's top line (client/README.md 6.14, the chat). The
    launchpad's framed header stays as it is.
    
    Not the look's: telling a box from another engine. The TUI knows it
    when the box starts it, or from the link file the box writes.
    
    Look-request: tui-chat-title-below
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

